-- Q977: International Tax [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 951A(b), net GILTI equals aggregate tested income from all CFCs minus the net deemed tangible income return (DTIR). DTIR is 10% of aggregate QBAI: 10% x $20,000,000 = $2,000,000. Net GILTI = $5,000,000 minus $2,000,000 = $3,000,000. A domestic C corporation may then claim a 50% Section 250 deduction on this amount.
Wrong (A): $5,000,000 ignores the QBAI offset entirely and treats all tested income as GILTI.
Wrong (C): $2,000,000 is the DTIR offset amount, not the net GILTI inclusion.
Wrong (D): QBAI of $50,000,000 or more would be needed to fully shelter $5,000,000 of tested income, which is not the case here.$EXPL$
